            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @chaul@amperecomputing.com,\n\nI am continuing the state sensor work from topic pldm_state_sensor_support in the following link:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/85039\n\nFollowing the suggestion by the @manojkiran.eda@gmail.com in the review comments in 85039, I would like to align our implementation rather than keep 2 parallel implementation. I have pushed a design proposal here that covers your externally mapped approach and the self-describing approach from 85039.\n\nPlease walk through the docs and check if you have any concern or missing information that I didn't catch, and feel free to upload your suggestion if you have any. \n\nThanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't especially stick with the direction that state sensor objects are to be created by other services. Historically to prevent the need to propose State interface to D-Bus, I followed IBM design, in which D-Bus objects are created by pldmd from the entity association PDRs, not from the sensor PDR itself.\n\nI see that you updated your patch which is great."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Understood! For that, I have updated the design and have pushed a new patchset (PS8) for that. Hopefully that aligns with your thought.\n\nThanks for the reviewing as well!"
                }
            ],
