                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Apologizes for the confusing statement. That was the previous design which I have abandoned.\nI have updated the document in PS8 and there should be no parent object anymore.\nThe reason I abandon this is because I just noticed the design was against the sensor-architecture stated in the following link:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/6dfd3bb55bcb827d38ce6ce11b84913596aa23ca/architecture/sensor-architecture.md?plain=1#L19\n\nThe design proposal in PS8 uses flattened approaches to expose the state set/component sensor as a single dbus-object similar to numeric sensor.\n\nIn addition, the `<label>` in component state sensor has a slightly different naming rule compared to numeric sensor otherwise there could be naming conflict in the case where a composite state sensor having multiple component sensor with identical state set type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
                    "line": 538,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we switch to the term \"component sensor\" or something to distinguish with the offset of that component sensor as later used."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
                    "line": 538,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, I have modified the term `offset` to `component sensor` for better understanding. Thanks for acknowledging."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
                    "line": 589,
                    "reviewer": {
